From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:32:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: FORK_BIG only while the machine is
 narrow; optional start lift

FORK_BIG starts a new task on an idle CPU of the highest capacity. On the
M4 MacBook Pro this brings a single unhinted memory copy thread from
61-77 to 93-94.5 GB/s, but a 10-thread fixed-time CPU test lost 7 points
with it, and the single-thread triad stayed at 72 GB/s against 96 with a
uclamp_min hint on the same P cores.

Apply FORK_BIG only while fewer tasks run than there are CPUs of the
highest capacity, so a wide fork is spread by the usual slow path.

Add the debugfs knob fork_big_lift (default 0; not a sched feature: the
feature mask is full): a new task that starts on a CPU of the highest
capacity it may use starts with that CPU's whole spare capacity as its
utilization instead of half of it, so schedutil asks for the top clock
at once instead of ramping over the task's first tens of milliseconds.

FORK_BIG and fork_big_lift are both off by default.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 kernel/sched/debug.c |  1 +
 kernel/sched/fair.c  | 37 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 kernel/sched/sched.h |  1 +
 3 files changed, 38 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/debug.c b/kernel/sched/debug.c
index 806d90e304..5f28fbaaff 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/debug.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/debug.c
@@ -730,6 +730,7 @@ static __init int sched_init_debug(void)
 	debugfs_create_u32("migration_cost_ns", 0644, debugfs_sched, &sysctl_sched_migration_cost);
 	debugfs_create_u32("nr_migrate", 0644, debugfs_sched, &sysctl_sched_nr_migrate);
 	debugfs_create_u32("misfit_runtime_ns", 0644, debugfs_sched, &sysctl_sched_misfit_runtime);
+	debugfs_create_u32("fork_big_lift", 0644, debugfs_sched, &sysctl_sched_fork_big_lift);
 
 	sched_domains_mutex_lock();
 	update_sched_domain_debugfs();
diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index 98d4719523..6e2a23137e 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -93,6 +93,14 @@ __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_migration_cost	= 500000UL;
  */
 __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_misfit_runtime	= 8000000UL;
 
+/*
+ * fork_big_lift: a new task that starts on a CPU of the highest capacity it
+ * may use starts with that CPU's spare capacity as its utilization, not half
+ * of it. (default: 0 = off; a debugfs knob, not a sched feature, because the
+ * feature mask is full)
+ */
+__read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_fork_big_lift;
+
 static int __init setup_sched_thermal_decay_shift(char *str)
 {
 	pr_warn("Ignoring the deprecated sched_thermal_decay_shift= option\n");
@@ -1404,6 +1412,16 @@ void post_init_entity_util_avg(struct task_struct *p)
 		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * fork_big_lift: on a CPU of the highest capacity the task may use, start
+	 * from the CPU's whole spare capacity, so that the frequency governor
+	 * does not ramp a CPU-bound new task up over tens of milliseconds.
+	 */
+	if (READ_ONCE(sysctl_sched_fork_big_lift) && sched_asym_cpucap_active() && cap > 0 &&
+	    !(p->flags & PF_KTHREAD) &&
+	    cpu_scale == (long)p->max_allowed_capacity)
+		sa->util_avg = 2 * cap;
+
 	sa->runnable_avg = sa->util_avg;
 }
 
@@ -9986,12 +10004,29 @@ static int select_idle_biggest(struct task_struct *p)
 	return -1;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Only while the machine is narrow: fewer tasks run than there are CPUs of
+ * the highest capacity. A wide fork (a pool of workers) is then spread by
+ * the usual slow path instead of being started on the big CPUs first.
+ */
+static bool fork_big_narrow(struct task_struct *p)
+{
+	unsigned int big = 0;
+	int cpu;
+
+	for_each_cpu_and(cpu, p->cpus_ptr, cpu_active_mask)
+		if (arch_scale_cpu_capacity(cpu) == p->max_allowed_capacity)
+			big++;
+	return nr_running() < big;
+}
+
 static inline bool fork_big_candidate(struct task_struct *p, int wake_flags)
 {
 	return (wake_flags & (WF_FORK | WF_EXEC)) && sched_feat(FORK_BIG) &&
 	       sched_asym_cpucap_active() && !(p->flags & PF_KTHREAD) &&
 	       !task_has_idle_policy(p) &&
-	       uclamp_eff_value(p, UCLAMP_MAX) >= p->max_allowed_capacity;
+	       uclamp_eff_value(p, UCLAMP_MAX) >= p->max_allowed_capacity &&
+	       fork_big_narrow(p);
 }
 
 static int
diff --git a/kernel/sched/sched.h b/kernel/sched/sched.h
index a0b694dafa..8948249996 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/sched.h
+++ b/kernel/sched/sched.h
@@ -3159,6 +3159,7 @@ static inline void attach_one_task(struct rq *rq, struct task_struct *p)
 extern __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_nr_migrate;
 extern __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_migration_cost;
 extern __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_misfit_runtime;
+extern __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_fork_big_lift;
 
 extern unsigned int sysctl_sched_base_slice;
 
-- 
2.43.0

